From 87fe489e5ab5b196a11901b68683f2efc9ea88f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:03:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 014/114] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350-oneplus: QCA6490 Wi-Fi/BT
 via WCN6855 power sequencer

Replace the out-of-tree qca6490_pd hack with the upstream qcom,wcn6855-pmu
power sequencer (rails per the downstream cnss-qca6490 node: aon/dig
0.952V, rfa1 1.88V, rfa2 1.35V, io 1.8V, antenna switch always-on), add the
PCIe root port with the wifi@0 endpoint, switch Bluetooth to
qcom,wcn6855-bt, and fix PERST# polarity (active low). Bluetooth works;
the PCIe link trains Gen3 and enumerates 17cb:1103.

Also let PCI_PWRCTRL_PWRSEQ be built in so the endpoint is powered before
link training.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-oneplus-common.dtsi  | 147 ++++++++++++------
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-oneplus-lemonade.dts |   9 --
 .../dts/qcom/sm8350-oneplus-lemonadep.dts     |   5 -
 drivers/pci/pwrctrl/Kconfig                   |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 62 deletions(-)

